# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, regardless of the platform a
# contributor generates them on. Without this the study data lands in the repo
# with whatever endings the generating machine used: Python's csv writer emits
# CRLF on every platform, while write_text() emits LF on Linux and CRLF on
# Windows, so the CSVs and the .txt/.md artefacts end up disagreeing with each
# other inside the same commit. A clean rebuild then shows half the outputs as
# modified when nothing has actually changed, which is exactly the kind of noise
# that makes a diff useless for review.
* text=auto

*.png binary
*.pbix binary
